The happy assertion-bearing test verified adoption of the same terminal,
terminal/process incarnations, PID and process start token, raw tail bytes and
offset range, and replay of an exit with final offset 8 until the core
acknowledges that offset. The failure assertion-bearing test verified
unsupported generation 999 without changing retained state, stale incarnation
rejection, malformed frame rejection, and rejection of payloads above 16 MiB.
Separate assertions cover stable frame-header bytes and write-grant, fence,
and acknowledgement epochs.
